data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Need fix layout in src/App.jsx. We already had a wrapper div inside Page with flex centering. But apparently page content area not filling viewport height. We need make Page wrapper (or direct child of AppShell around Page) a flex container with flex: 1 1 auto, display flex, alignItems center, justifyContent center, and fill remaining height. The current wrapper inside Page has style flex:1 display:flex etc. But Page itself is main and has flex:1? Actually AppShell CSS sets main flex:1. Page is main and has classes display flex column, flex:1 (from .cs-component-page-3). So Page itself is flex container column, flex 1, but we need center content. We can add className or style to Page to make it center with justifyContent center and alignItems center. But Page has its own display flex column. Setting justifyContent/alignItems via style would override? Inline style allowed. But the d003 suggests making the Page wrapper (or direct child of AppShell around Page) a flex container with flex:1 1 auto, display flex, alignItems center, justifyContent center. So easiest: wrap Page in a div (direct child of AppShell) with those styles. Or add style to Page component: Page accepts HTMLAttributes, so style prop. But Page renders \u003cmain\u003e with className .cs-component-page-1 (display flex column). If we add style alignItems/justifyContent, it should work, plus Page already flex:1 due to class .cs-component-page-3? Wait .cs-component-page-3 sets flex:1 1 0%. Yes Page has flex:1 because scroll=true default. So we can add style={{ alignItems: \"center\", justifyContent: \"center\" }} to Page. But d003 says \"making the Page wrapper (or a direct child of AppShell around Page) a flex container with flex: 1 1 auto, display: flex, alignItems: center, and justifyContent: center. Ensure the wrapper itself grows to fill the remaining viewport height after the Header.\" So a direct child of AppShell around Page (i.e., a div wrapping Page) with those styles. Because AppShell CSS already makes `\u003cmain\u003e` flex:1, but if we wrap Page in a div with flex:1, that div will fill remaining height. Page inside could also flex center. Let's implement as a div around Page with style as specified, and maybe remove inner wrapper. Let's read current App.jsx."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959266,"id":"chatcmpl-20dc5a20954540959401c78fdbe59a3c","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

